Part 2: API Case Study
Selected Tasks
Task 1: Basic API Development with Swagger

Overview

For this section, I focused on designing a simple User Management API.

Instead of overcomplicating the solution, I approached it from a business and integration perspective — defining clear endpoints, expected inputs/outputs, and ensuring proper validation and error handling.

The goal was to design something that is:

Easy to understand
Scalable
Practical for real-world use
API Design: User Management System
Base URL
/api/v1
Endpoints Overview
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/users	Create a user
GET	/users/{id}	Retrieve user details
PUT	/users/{id}	Update user
DELETE	/users/{id}	Delete user
1. Create User
Endpoint
POST /users
Request Body
{
  "name": "Harry",
  "email": "harry34704@outlook.com"
}
Success Response (201 Created)
{
  "id": 101,
  "name": "Harry",
  "email": "harry34704@outlook.com",
  "created_at": "2026-03-27"
}
2. Get User
Endpoint
GET /users/{id}
Example
GET /users/101
Response (200 OK)
{
  "id": 101,
  "name": "harry",
  "email": "harry34704@outlook.com"
}
3. Update User
Endpoint
PUT /users/{id}
Request Body
{
  "name": "Hanay Munyai",
  "email": "harry34704@outlook.com"
}
Response (200 OK)
{
  "message": "User updated successfully"
}
4. Delete User
Endpoint
DELETE /users/{id}
Response (200 OK)
{
  "message": "User deleted successfully"
}



